[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73349"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/6393810d90b8d340dbde041c43cb7e146cb59fedfcfd4a678827d291ea502b00.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,4]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,4).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-73354"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/029a51dccba9f1ec927c820fb8adb72e926b88a881f4646090ac651ef29da271.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on $(-5,3).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection/e88916322dda9c27357e36c3938c1e4b0534b235d9c5f2372254ba5822629cc5" :answer/id #uuid "f52e26a5-956a-5bea-893d-18bfc7eb0051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(c)=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection/401db3a7dff70100ab6d99dae340a89ccd6a50f658c059a994a2a9badcc19722" :answer/id #uuid "f9834fc1-68ab-5c9f-98d1-9318078c44c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(c)=\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection/8d2bb04d020a65234cb7633647e830376f2ce15b8b1661c8600ca908beb17847" :answer/id #uuid "8f371631-8e29-5248-b657-ca3cc7123192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=-\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection/6950ce0c96be12fbd5d0d79cfef1210f4c59984ac87f7f2c5d20a3278334442e" :answer/id #uuid "0133ec9f-af36-5f92-a87d-38a6cbff465b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection/f2e92858bad9bbc2123de0fc0d08dcfe763df5252e534574c8fb8a98c0692951" :answer/id #uuid "3dd23e03-9c78-58d1-b589-b5dd93ff6c47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dcca2840-f4f8-5f50-b28d-ce12b2abd672" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125236/selection/f2e92858bad9bbc2123de0fc0d08dcfe763df5252e534574c8fb8a98c0692951" :answer-field/choices ["q-125236/selection/e88916322dda9c27357e36c3938c1e4b0534b235d9c5f2372254ba5822629cc5" "q-125236/selection/401db3a7dff70100ab6d99dae340a89ccd6a50f658c059a994a2a9badcc19722" "q-125236/selection/8d2bb04d020a65234cb7633647e830376f2ce15b8b1661c8600ca908beb17847" "q-125236/selection/6950ce0c96be12fbd5d0d79cfef1210f4c59984ac87f7f2c5d20a3278334442e" "q-125236/selection/f2e92858bad9bbc2123de0fc0d08dcfe763df5252e534574c8fb8a98c0692951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125236" :question/id #uuid "b24b1f9d-0768-54a7-a045-f1ebf26ee3d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-125236" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/a7a36a62dcbbe0a0d67b9ccc8517eb7584e75d41d01227141229da3eed583500.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-3,4]$ and differentiable on $(-3,4).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-3,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following:\n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-3$ and $b=4.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(4)-f(-3)}{4-(-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-3)}{4+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-3,4)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{4}{7}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125236/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8756e5e-3ce4-5c02-8700-8e2f3fa81e9b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125236"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48554"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/429c0a3eb7a6b1b0a99fba09eb7dd062f645669e99d39a919dc369467b4c373d.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-2,4]$ and differentiable on $(-2,4).$ Complete the sentence below.\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-2,4)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :question/worked-solution "Given that $f(x)$ is continuous on $[a,b]$ and differentiable on  $(a,b)$, the mean value theorem states the following:\n\n*There exists a point $c\\in (a,b)$ such that*\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-2$ and $b=4.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(4)-f(-2)}{4-(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-4}{4+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complete sentence is as follows:\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-2,4)$ such that ${f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{3}.$*" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-125237"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/74850221ee168c6911ee5b6c319d2128f67149f81790528940822e253905fc0f.png)\n\nThe function $y=f(x)$ above is continuous on the interval $[-5,3]$ and differentiable on  $(-5,3).$  What is the missing part of the sentence in the statement below?\n\n*The mean value theorem states that there exists a point $c\\in (-5,3)$ such that $\\text{_______}\\,.$ *" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "f0b611b5-e022-58ac-a112-ce62a70c2b8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection/a9182785b92b59cb786be37f100bf45b24ebedcd17722afa0b5b2d4c10e62ff5" :answer/id #uuid "3fb8ec51-6a21-586a-abc8-f5f79feff775" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{log}_{2}⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection/ab62ab9e1d94fcc0d30be09b2c04709ee00089e0801267640885ada6a43da71e" :answer/id #uuid "0a82503b-99f4-5f08-b0d6-950d392a1c2f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection/b4cf5553e3860d836be0f41b8799020db89df3f4d7d90f60365a26980d9b4919" :answer/id #uuid "7799dac2-a0a3-5e9f-b2fe-9bb31e63aafb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "339c763a-b505-5cb6-94d0-384a3549bfe8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d74fb0c-5981-5b86-a6a9-9ef17f6aad53" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125251/selection/b4cf5553e3860d836be0f41b8799020db89df3f4d7d90f60365a26980d9b4919" :answer-field/choices ["q-125251/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-125251/selection/a9182785b92b59cb786be37f100bf45b24ebedcd17722afa0b5b2d4c10e62ff5" "q-125251/selection/ab62ab9e1d94fcc0d30be09b2c04709ee00089e0801267640885ada6a43da71e" "q-125251/selection/b4cf5553e3860d836be0f41b8799020db89df3f4d7d90f60365a26980d9b4919" "q-125251/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125251" :question/id #uuid "9c2ace5b-4a86-5d8b-a101-1aeed1dde583" :question/math-academy-id "q-125251" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡x$ on the interval $[4,16].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[4,16]$ and differentiable on $(4,16),$ hence, we can apply the Mean Value Theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (4,16)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=4$ and $b=16$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(16)-f(4)}{16-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(16)-{log}_{2}⁡(4)}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ c & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125251/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125251"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345316/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "1df5aaa6-3a50-569b-b90f-432bb3994961" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345316/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ddda1bce-689e-5238-ba06-1b7f090e6042" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345316/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-345316/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345316" :question/id #uuid "1627d046-23a7-5910-b67c-f60a8b23fe62" :question/math-academy-id "q-345316" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for  $f(x)={x}^{2}+1$ on the interval $[-1,3].$\n\n$c=$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-1,3]$ and differentiable on $(-1,3),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem.  \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (-1,3)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=-1$ and $b=3$ into the above gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(3)-f(-1)}{3-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{({3}^{2}+1)-((-1)^{2}+1)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-2}{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1)=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2c & =2 \\\\ c & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345316/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection/84736ab45fae4fbf32a66bc98906d9921687e72f75bede2b186ec59b0558ac2e" :answer/id #uuid "03aad5e8-ea9f-5fa6-a7cf-d1c1622aa435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection/219f54fb32109a80aef494ebda96f07e0b414f1b98a5dff7a50726a630ea947c" :answer/id #uuid "daa29262-3da5-53a0-a201-c2bfbbfde6ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection/d6505bbef4eba7be9787cdfc88eb540f833229bcc1cbc3012ae2150760c4f776" :answer/id #uuid "995151b3-0f0f-5b7f-b59f-f4eed6526c09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36}{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection/d0956dff3dcd0b4ab493380de13d811e31c02e35ba86aaa4a11a750f8b6c04f2" :answer/id #uuid "8bcd3579-8d58-5d07-99d3-f04035f5b57b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection/c11efa80c15d1941254a27c37db155f5cdf388cb9fd51dfcfa8d451e722f987b" :answer/id #uuid "e19f8e8e-d058-5637-96ec-fc4a145adffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{72}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50d2304d-ce4d-54fe-ba1d-b0010c6f58e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-125252/selection/d0956dff3dcd0b4ab493380de13d811e31c02e35ba86aaa4a11a750f8b6c04f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-125252/selection/84736ab45fae4fbf32a66bc98906d9921687e72f75bede2b186ec59b0558ac2e" "q-125252/selection/219f54fb32109a80aef494ebda96f07e0b414f1b98a5dff7a50726a630ea947c" "q-125252/selection/d6505bbef4eba7be9787cdfc88eb540f833229bcc1cbc3012ae2150760c4f776" "q-125252/selection/d0956dff3dcd0b4ab493380de13d811e31c02e35ba86aaa4a11a750f8b6c04f2" "q-125252/selection/c11efa80c15d1941254a27c37db155f5cdf388cb9fd51dfcfa8d451e722f987b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-125252" :question/id #uuid "a95efa0b-db7f-50aa-a72c-805b5062f119" :question/math-academy-id "q-125252" :question/problem "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for $f(x)={log}_{3}⁡x$ on the interval $[9,81].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[9,81]$ and differentiable on $(9,81),$ hence, we can apply the Mean Value Theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (9,81)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=9$ and $b=81$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(81)-f(9)}{81-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(81)-{log}_{3}⁡(9)}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{c\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} & =\\frac{1}{36} \\\\ c & =\\frac{36}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-125252/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-125252"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer/id #uuid "a9bd7471-e64a-5857-9381-24b302e93a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection/e23f9ea338f175b3f5a7621b94518bec0d179d6cb526e41f6e659cfd147c4d14" :answer/id #uuid "567b304d-e1c6-554e-a029-d61730bc21ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "1679c9c9-d05c-5963-bee8-c993282c6f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "6d9e14f1-eaa2-5dbd-886b-f1d35503555c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "29947c6a-4526-5c3b-b860-95d1678c90df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac508cf5-09b0-5ef4-b8e5-58e91c27a935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-2317/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" :answer-field/choices ["q-2317/selection/a05724295bc0340162295da21b8749cd336584b7c76ed9f6810ddb03e7f98d00" "q-2317/selection/e23f9ea338f175b3f5a7621b94518bec0d179d6cb526e41f6e659cfd147c4d14" "q-2317/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-2317/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-2317/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-2317" :question/id #uuid "8aa60ea3-4337-579e-bd3a-a287bb61ea84" :question/math-academy-id "q-2317" :question/problem "Find the values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for  $f(x)={x}^{3}$ on the interval $[0,1].$" :question/worked-solution "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,1]$ and differentiable on $(0,1),$ hence we can apply the mean value theorem. \n\nSo, the mean value theorem states that there exists a $c\\in (0,1)$ such that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=\\frac{f(b)-f(a)}{b-a}.\n$$\n\nPlugging in $a=0$ and $b=1$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(c) & =\\frac{f(1)-f(0)}{1-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{3}-{0}^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})=3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(c)=3{c}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $c\\in (0,1)$, we discard the negative value, therefore $c=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-2317/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3f4a987-4c82-55b0-aa48-923ee6c0417e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-2317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127009/selection/a61a9ede3f23b729f546b3a789be54441c68e0df59d468a7aa639cec3cb4515d" :answer/id #uuid "27424c7d-955b-50f9-be2d-6d0fc7550bff" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/83fffb6e46362e577cdc45bff6123555e070dc539505522ff134f2859954f9b2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127009/selection/4812403ca3c39687572e1d94ca5db08c75f80c4b32b5ea4e66fadb992d7e6298" :answer/id #uuid "1b18e931-00c3-5105-9ffc-fde99764b658" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/c30de46f9f22348af7a80c808ee8374fee195f44d3333c66c10803b42866a8cf.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127009/selection/b85b93d7e1ec0c971df1820a05fd25a98bf52317d71ca2b9c0c69276f1a216de" :answer/id #uuid "e6a0089f-a6a3-5e84-9576-a32315a63212" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074895/assets/2eba8ffb2094fab214cdebc0459ac6849c6bc2c37ac0f9bbd3fe026e44334800.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127009/selection/7925c2943f54e501f565951233b3abd7e02654d86cc94de33c9eebcf7eb2ad63" :answer/id #uuid "e15fc95e-f3f4-5585-b1ba-8bd6a58c8d70" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/1